  "narrative": "<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Short impact summary</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">This Dryad dataset is showing early but real reuse: it has 150 downloads, 746 views, one scholarly citation, and two documented downstream reuse signals. Together, these indicate that the data are being consulted and incorporated into later work, even though the citation record is still small.</p>\n<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Full narrative</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">The dataset supports a 2017 study on holozoan phylogeny and the evolutionary origins of animal signaling systems, a topic at the intersection of phylogenetics, evolutionary biology, and comparative genomics. Its strongest impact signal is active use: repository metrics show sustained interest with 746 views and 150 downloads, suggesting the data continue to attract attention beyond the original publication.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Scholarly uptake is visible but still early. OpenAlex records one citation, and Crossref data-citation records show the dataset being cited as a dataset in later journal articles. That pattern points to direct reuse rather than only conceptual reference, which is especially meaningful for a data resource hosted in Dryad.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Reuse evidence also appears in the downstream record, where two reuse signals are captured, including one article and one Biomedical Article mention. The citing landscape is narrow at present, with the single documented citing work appearing in eLife, so the record supports a cautious interpretation: the dataset is already part of the literature, but its broader citation footprint is still developing.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Stewardship signals strengthen the case for accessibility and persistence. The dataset is preserved in Dryad, an open repository with DOI-based identification, and related dataset links indicate that the underlying materials are distributed across persistent records. Public discourse and social attention are not captured in the available archive here, so the impact story rests primarily on repository use and emerging scholarly reuse.</p>",
